# Citation metadata for Sarimax.jl. GitHub shows it as "Cite this repository"; Zenodo's
# GitHub integration reads .zenodo.json for the archived release.
#
# The version DOIs of the software and data records are added once the Zenodo records are
# published.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use Sarimax.jl, please cite the software and the article below. To cite the exact
  code and data used for the article's results, cite the version DOIs of the archived
  release and of the experimental-artifact record (see replication/ijf-2026/README.md).
title: "Sarimax.jl: optimization-based SARIMAX modeling in Julia"
type: software
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-09-12"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/LAMPSPUC/Sarimax.jl"
url: "https://lampspuc.github.io/Sarimax.jl/dev/"
abstract: >-
  Sarimax.jl estimates SARIMA and SARIMAX models by formulating them as explicit JuMP
  optimization problems: coefficients and residuals are decision variables, the model
  dynamics are constraints, and the objective function, coefficient constraints,
  regularization and solver (local, such as Ipopt, or global, such as SCIP) are
  user-selectable.
keywords:
  - time series
  - forecasting
  - SARIMAX
  - ARIMA
  - mathematical optimization
  - JuMP
  - Julia
